                </xsd:documentation>
                        </xsd:annotation>
                    </xsd:element>
                    <xsd:element name="SystemTripID" type="cis:KeyStringType" minOccurs="0">
                        <xsd:annotation>
                            <xsd:documentation>
                    The system Trip ID for which asset candidates should be retrieved.One of load ID or Trip ID should be given as input.
                </xsd:documentation>
                        </xsd:annotation>
                    </xsd:element>
                    <xsd:element name="AssetTypes" type="cis:ParameterType" minOccurs="0">
                        <xsd:annotation>
                            <xsd:documentation>
                    A list of comma separated Asset types. User can pass any active asset types. Invalid/inactive asset types will be ignored. When not provided all active asset types will be considered.
                </xsd:documentation>
                        </xsd:annotation>
                    </xsd:element>
                    <xsd:element name="NearbyAssetLimit" type="cis:NearbyAssetLimitType" minOccurs="0">
                        <xsd:annotation>
                            <xsd:documentation>
                    Radial distance in user UOM to limit driver asset type candidates. Optional. When passed it should be positive integer value. When not passed, distance filtering is not applied.
                </xsd:documentation>
                        </xsd:annotation>
                    </xsd:element>
                    <xsd:element name="IncludeEligibleEntriesFlag" type="xsd:boolean" minOccurs="0">
                        <xsd:annotation>
                            <xsd:documentation>
                    Indicates whether all eligible entries are to be included. One of these three flags should be true.One of these three(IncludeEligibleEntriesFlag, IncludeEntriesRequireOverrideFlag, IncludeIneligibleEntriesFlag) flags should be true. Defaults to true.
                </xsd:documentation>
                        </xsd:annotation>
                    </xsd:element>
                    <xsd:element name="IncludeEntriesRequireOverrideFlag" type="xsd:boolean" minOccurs="0">
                        <xsd:annotation>
                            <xsd:documentation>
                    Indicates whether all entries that require an override are to be included.One of these three(IncludeEligibleEntriesFlag, IncludeEntriesRequireOverrideFlag, IncludeIneligibleEntriesFlag) flags should be true. Defaults to false.
                </xsd:documentation>
                        </xsd:annotation>
                    </xsd:element>
                    <xsd:element name="IncludeIneligibleEntriesFlag" type="xsd:boolean" minOccurs="0">
                        <xsd:annotation>
                            <xsd:documentation>
                    Indicates whether all ineligible entries are to be included.One of these three(IncludeEligibleEntriesFlag, IncludeEntriesRequireOverrideFlag, IncludeIneligibleEntriesFlag) flags should be true. Defaults to false.
                </xsd:documentation>
                        </xsd:annotation>
                    </xsd:element>
                </xsd:sequence>
