                        <xsd:annotation>
                            <xsd:documentation>
					The load leg schedule ID chosen by user as the starting point of this asset assignment; used to mark the beginning of where the asset is an active part of a load or trip assignment; selection results in auto-population of related start location fields (ID, type, name and address) and stop ID from the associated load schedule entry; not populated when the assignment is unassociated; when populated, assignment validations are performed beginning with this load schedule ID; when not populated, validations are performed beginning with the start stop ID (if populated), or from the beginning of the associated load or trip.
				</xsd:documentation>
                        </xsd:annotation>
                    </xsd:element>
                    <xsd:element name="SystemEndLoadScheduleID" type="cis:KeyStringType" minOccurs="0">
                        <xsd:annotation>
                            <xsd:documentation>
					The load leg schedule ID chosen by user as the ending point of this asset assignment; used to mark the end of where the asset is an active part of a load or trip assignment; selection results in auto-population of related end location fields (ID, type, name and address) and stop ID from the associated load schedule entry; not populated when the assignment is unassociated; when populated, assignment validations are performed until this load schedule ID; when not populated, validations are performed until the end stop ID (if populated), or until the end of the associated load or trip.
				</xsd:documentation>
                        </xsd:annotation>
                    </xsd:element>
                    <xsd:element name="SystemStartStopID" type="cis:KeyStringType" minOccurs="0">
                        <xsd:annotation>
                            <xsd:documentation>
					The stop ID explicitly chosen by user as the starting point of this asset assignment, or the stop ID associated with the start load schedule ID, if populated; used to mark where the asset begins being an active part of a load or trip assignment; selection results in auto-population of related start location fields (ID, type, name, address) from the associated stop entry; not populated when the assignment is unassociated; when populated, assignment validations are performed beginning with this stop ID; when not populated, validations are performed from the start of the associated load or trip.
				</xsd:documentation>
                        </xsd:annotation>
                    </xsd:element>
                    <xsd:element name="SystemEndStopID" type="cis:KeyStringType" minOccurs="0">
                        <xsd:annotation>
                            <xsd:documentation>
					The stop ID explicitly chosen by user as the ending point of this asset assignment, or the stop ID associated with the end load schedule ID, if populated; used to mark where the asset ends being an active part of a load or trip assignment; selection results in auto-population of related end location fields (ID, type, name, address) from the associated stop entry; not populated when the assignment is unassociated; when populated, assignment validations are performed until this stop ID; when not populated, validations are performed until the end of the associated load or trip.
				</xsd:documentation>
                        </xsd:annotation>
                    </xsd:element>
                </xsd:sequence>
            </xsd:complexType>
