                        </xsd:annotation>
                    </xsd:element>
                    <xsd:element name="SchedulingModeEnumVal" type="cis:SchedulingModeEnumValType" minOccurs="0">
                        <xsd:annotation>
                            <xsd:documentation>
					Controls the scheduling mode for a load that is being executed this flag is applicable only when scheduling is active and a load/trip has reached the point where execution scheduling is applicable when scheduling is performed using planning mode, the earliest possible pickup from date/time for the shipments being picked at the load's first stop or the load's scheduled date/time, whichever is later, will be used as the earliest schedule date/time and all lead times for the carrier and locations will be observed using planning mode, the computed start date/time for the load could be later than the earliest schedule date/time when scheduling is performed using confirmation mode, the shipped date/time for the load will be used as the start date/time for scheduling and lead times will not be observed when scheduling is performed using execution mode, user reported actual times are used as the basis to compute the remaining itinerary that has not been reported scheduling will always be performed using planning mode for loads that have not had any execution-oriented activity for trips, determination is based on the status of the first load on the trip's itinerary.
				</xsd:documentation>
                        </xsd:annotation>
                    </xsd:element>
                    <xsd:element name="SchedulingModeEnumDescr" type="xsd:string" minOccurs="0">
                        <xsd:annotation>
                            <xsd:documentation>
					Description for SchedulingModeEnumVal. Read-only. Available only through UI-oriented APIs.
				</xsd:documentation>
                        </xsd:annotation>
                    </xsd:element>
