                        <xsd:element name="ShipmentIDType" type="cis:ShipmentIdEnumValType" minOccurs="0">
                            <xsd:annotation>
                                <xsd:documentation>
                    An enumerated value defining how the shipment should be identified.
                    
                        SI_NULL - No shipments are retrieved.
                        
                        SI_ID - The shipments to be identified by their IDs.
                        
                        SI_NUM - The shipments to be identified by their shipment numbers.
                        
                        SI_RFRC - The shipments to be identified by their reference numbers.
                        
                        SI_RFRC_DIV - The shipments to be identified by their reference numbers and Division ID.
                            If a user is not restricted to a division, then a division must be specified in the input. If a user is restricted to a division, then a division can be omitted or, if specified, should match the division to which the user is restricted.
                            
                        SI_TRKG_NUM - The shipments to be identified by their shipment tracking number. This is ShipmentDescription in the ShipmentType structure.
                        
                        SI_TRKG_NUM_DIV - The shipments to be identified by their shipment tracking number. This is ShipmentDescription in the ShipmentType structure.
                            If a user is not restricted to a division, then a division must be specified in the input. If a user is restricted to a division, then the division can be omitted or, if specified, it should match the division to which the user is restricted.
                            
                        SI_LEG_ID - The shipment legs to be identified by their shipment leg IDs.
                        
                        SI_BOL_NUM_CARR - The shipment legs to be identified by their Carrier Codes and Bill Of Lading Numbers.
