        <operation name="processShipmentOrderCancel">
            <documentation>Cancels shipments. The transaction may fail if Transportation Manager is unavailable, or if there is an error in the request. An error message will be published on the front bus.</documentation>
            <input message="cis:processShipmentOrderCancel"/>
            <output message="cis:processShipmentOrderCancelResponse"/>
            <fault name="CISFault" message="cis:OperationException"/>
        </operation>
        <operation name="processShipmentOrderCreate">
            <documentation>Creates new shipments and returns content according to the request. This operation may invoke Routing, Rating and Scheduling unless instructed otherwise in the input. The transaction may fail if Transportation Manager is unavailable, or if there is an error in the request. An error message will be published on the front bus.</documentation>
            <input message="cis:processShipmentOrderCreate"/>
            <output message="cis:processShipmentOrderCreateResponse"/>
            <fault name="CISFault" message="cis:OperationException"/>
        </operation>
        <operation name="processShipmentOrderDelete">
            <documentation>Deletes existing shipments. The shipments to be deleted can be identified by their Shipment ID, Shipment Tracking Number, a Reference Number, or a combination of Shipment Tracking Number, and Division or Reference Number, and Division. The transaction may fail if Transportation Manager is unavailable, or if there is an error in the request. An error message will be published on the front bus.</documentation>
            <input message="cis:processShipmentOrderDelete"/>
            <output message="cis:processShipmentOrderDeleteResponse"/>
            <fault name="CISFault" message="cis:OperationException"/>
        </operation>
        <operation name="processShipmentOrderRetrieve">
            <documentation>Retrieves content of shipments. The shipments to be retrieved can be identified by their Shipment ID, Shipment Tracking Number, a Reference Number, or a combination of Shipment Tracking Number, and Division or Reference Number, and Division. The transaction may fail if Transportation Manager is unavailable, or if there is an error in the request. An error message will be published on the front bus.</documentation>
            <input message="cis:processShipmentOrderRetrieve"/>
            <output message="cis:processShipmentOrderRetrieveResponse"/>
            <fault name="CISFault" message="cis:OperationException"/>
        </operation>
        <operation name="processShipmentOrderUpdate">
            <documentation>Modifies the content of existing shipments. The shipments to be modified can be identified by their Shipment ID, Shipment Tracking Number, a Reference Number, or a combination of Shipment Tracking Number, and Division or Reference Number, and Division. This operation may invoke Routing, Rating and Scheduling unless instructed otherwise in the input. The transaction may fail if Transportation Manager is unavailable, or if there is an error in the request. An error message will be published on the front bus.</documentation>
            <input message="cis:processShipmentOrderUpdate"/>
            <output message="cis:processShipmentOrderUpdateResponse"/>
            <fault name="CISFault" message="cis:OperationException"/>
        </operation>
        <operation name="processShipmentOrderMaintain">
            <documentation>Creates, updates and deletes shipments. This adaptor provides the functionality of the processShipmentOrderCreate, processShipmentOrderUpdate, and processShipmentOrderDelete adaptors. It processes the individual shipment create, update and delete requests using a single transaction. This operation may invoke Routing, Rating and Scheduling unless instructed otherwise in the input. The transaction may fail if Transportation Manager is unavailable, or if there is an error in the request. An error message will be published on the front bus. Expected Result: Shipments will be created, delete or updated in Transportation Manager. The request will succeed or fail as a single unit of work.</documentation>
            <input message="cis:processShipmentOrderMaintain"/>
            <output message="cis:processShipmentOrderMaintainResponse"/>
            <fault name="CISFault" message="cis:OperationException"/>
        </operation>
        <operation name="processShipmentContainerMaintain">
            <documentation>Adds, updates or deletes shipment containers for a shipment. This operation may invoke Routing, Rating and Scheduling unless instructed otherwise in the input. The transaction may fail if Transportation Manager is unavailable, or if there is an error in the request. An error message will be published on the front bus.</documentation>
            <input message="cis:processShipmentContainerMaintain"/>
            <output message="cis:processShipmentContainerMaintainResponse"/>
            <fault name="CISFault" message="cis:OperationException"/>
        </operation>
        <operation name="addPreBuiltLoad">
            <documentation>Creates pre-built loads. Based on the request, the operation will create the specified shipments, an empty load, and assign the shipment's shipment legs to the created load. The request has the following restrictions: The plan for a new load should be created in advance. Each shipment sent as part of this operation must have exactly one shipment leg, or the operation will fail. Each shipment sent as part of this operation is treated as a new shipment; it is not related back to existing shipments in Transportation Manager. The stops are built in Transportation Manager according to its rules. Routing, Rating and Scheduling will be invoked for the load in Transportation Manager. The plans under which all loads using this operation are created must already be in Transportation Manager and reference the same division as all the shipments sent as part of the operation. All shipments from one source may have the same division; therefore only one plan referring that division must be created in advance in Transportation Manager. The transaction may fail if Transportation Manager is unavailable, or if there is an error in the request. An error message will be published on the front bus.</documentation>
            <input message="cis:addPreBuiltLoad"/>
            <output message="cis:addPreBuiltLoadResponse"/>
            <fault name="CISFault" message="cis:OperationException"/>
        </operation>
        <operation name="processLoadCompositionUpdate">
            <documentation>Updates a load using the specified shipments. Based on the request, the operation will delete all shipments for the load, create the specified shipments, and assign the shipments' shipment legs to the load according to the pre-existing load itinerary. The request has the following restrictions: The load's status must be Tender Accepted. All shipment legs of the load must be first shipment legs of their respective shipments. Each shipment sent as part of this operation is treated as a new shipment; it is not related back to existing shipments in Transportation Manager. The new shipments cannot be created in Use for Planning Only mode. The stops are built in Transportation Manager according to its rules. The transaction may fail if Transportation Manager is unavailable, or if there is an error in the request. An error message will be published on the front bus.</documentation>
            <input message="cis:processLoadCompositionUpdate"/>
            <output message="cis:processLoadCompositionUpdateResponse"/>
            <fault name="CISFault" message="cis:OperationException"/>
        </operation>
        <operation name="processAssignToLoad">
            <documentation>Assigns existing shipment legs to an existing load. The transaction may fail if Transportation Manager is unavailable, or if there is an error in the request. An error message will be published on the front bus.</documentation>
            <input message="cis:processAssignToLoad"/>
            <output message="cis:processAssignToLoadResponse"/>
            <fault name="CISFault" message="cis:OperationException"/>
        </operation>
        <operation name="processAssignToPlannedLoad">
            <documentation>Adds shipment legs to a load that is in Planned or greater status. The transaction may fail if Transportation Manager is unavailable, or if there is an error in the request. An error message will be published on the front bus.</documentation>
            <input message="cis:processAssignToPlannedLoad"/>
            <output message="cis:processAssignToPlannedLoadResponse"/>
            <fault name="CISFault" message="cis:OperationException"/>
        </operation>
        <operation name="processRemoveFromPlannedLoad">
            <documentation>Removes shipment legs from a load that is in Planned or greater status. The transaction may fail if Transportation Manager is unavailable, or if there is an error in the request. An error message will be published on the front bus.</documentation>
            <input message="cis:processRemoveFromPlannedLoad"/>
            <output message="cis:processRemoveFromPlannedLoadResponse"/>
            <fault name="CISFault" message="cis:OperationException"/>
        </operation>
        <operation name="processSetLoadToPlanned">
            <documentation>Use processSetLoadToPlanned to advance an existing load with a status of Open to a status of Planned and remove the load from its associated plan. If the load does not currently have valid Routing, Rating and Scheduling information, the operation will invoke Routing, Rating and Scheduling for the load. After successfully being set to Planned status, the load might be tendered or submitted for Carrier Sequential Tendering based on the Auto Tender setting in Global Defaults. You can successfully set a load to Planned status, but still fail to tender it or to submit it for Carrier Sequential Tendering. This is because the two operations are done in separate transactions. The transaction may fail if Transportation Manager is unavailable, or if there is an error in the request. An error message will be published on the front bus.</documentation>
            <input message="cis:processSetLoadToPlanned"/>
            <output message="cis:processSetLoadToPlannedResponse"/>
            <fault name="CISFault" message="cis:OperationException"/>
        </operation>
        <operation name="processPlan">
            <documentation>Creates load plans. The transaction may fail if Transportation Manager is unavailable, or if there is an error in the request. An error message will be published on the front bus.</documentation>
            <input message="cis:processPlan"/>
            <output message="cis:processPlanResponse"/>
            <fault name="CISFault" message="cis:OperationException"/>
        </operation>
        <operation name="processGetPossibleCharges">
            <documentation>Retrieves a list of possible charges using specific criteria. The transaction may fail if Transportation Manager is unavailable, or if there is an error in the request. An error message will be published on the front bus.</documentation>
            <input message="cis:processGetPossibleCharges"/>
            <output message="cis:processGetPossibleChargesResponse"/>
            <fault name="CISFault" message="cis:OperationException"/>
        </operation>
        <operation name="processRateQuotation">
            <documentation>Retrieves a set of valid lanes and the cost of each lane for the rate quotation request, in increasing order of shipping costs. This operation may invoke Routing, Rating and Scheduling. The transaction may fail if Transportation Manager is unavailable, or if there is an error in the request. An error message will be published on the front bus.</documentation>
            <input message="cis:processRateQuotation"/>
            <output message="cis:processRateQuotationResponse"/>
            <fault name="CISFault" message="cis:OperationException"/>
        </operation>
        <operation name="processRateQuotationRetrieve">
            <documentation>Retrieves existing rate quotation(s). The transaction may fail if Transportation Manager is unavailable, or if there is an error in the request. An error message will be published on the front bus.</documentation>
            <input message="cis:processRateQuotationRetrieve"/>
            <output message="cis:processRateQuotationRetrieveResponse"/>
            <fault name="CISFault" message="cis:OperationException"/>
        </operation>
        <operation name="processRateQuotationUpdate">
            <documentation>Updates existing rate quotation(s). The transaction may fail if Transportation Manager is unavailable, or if there is an error in the request. An error message will be published on the front bus.</documentation>
            <input message="cis:processRateQuotationUpdate"/>
            <output message="cis:processRateQuotationUpdateResponse"/>
            <fault name="CISFault" message="cis:OperationException"/>
        </operation>
        <operation name="processRateQuotationDelete">
            <documentation>Deletes existing rate quotation(s). The transaction may fail if Transportation Manager is unavailable, or if there is an error in the request. An error message will be published on the front bus.</documentation>
            <input message="cis:processRateQuotationDelete"/>
            <output message="cis:processRateQuotationDeleteResponse"/>
            <fault name="CISFault" message="cis:OperationException"/>
        </operation>
        <operation name="processRateQuotationSetStatus">
            <documentation>Activates or closes existing rate quotation(s). The transaction may fail if Transportation Manager is unavailable, or if there is an error in the request. An error message will be published on the front bus.</documentation>
            <input message="cis:processRateQuotationSetStatus"/>
            <output message="cis:processRateQuotationSetStatusResponse"/>
            <fault name="CISFault" message="cis:OperationException"/>
        </operation>
        <operation name="processLoadCreate">
            <documentation>Creates an empty load. The transaction may fail if Transportation Manager is unavailable, or if there is an error in the request. An error message will be published on the front bus.</documentation>
            <input message="cis:processLoadCreate"/>
            <output message="cis:processLoadCreateResponse"/>
            <fault name="CISFault" message="cis:OperationException"/>
        </operation>
        <operation name="processTender">
            <documentation>Advances the status from Planned to Tendered for a load or for loads of a trip. AutoAcceptControlEnumVal applies to each entry in the list. To tender a load, it must be in Planned status. The system checks the rating of the load or trip to ensure it is still valid. (Rating is the calculation of freight charges for shipments, shipment legs or loads.) The system takes into consideration that the load may have been set to Planned since it was last rated. Also, you may have specified new carrier, service, equipment type or domicile for the load tender or trip tender. If the Routing, Rating and Scheduling information is not valid for the load or trip, Routing, Rating and Scheduling may be invoked. The status of the load(s) might be promoted further to Tender Accepted based on the value of AutoAcceptControlEnumVal. The transaction may fail if Transportation Manager is unavailable, or if there is an error in the request. An error message will be published on the front bus.</documentation>
            <input message="cis:processTender"/>
            <output message="cis:processTenderResponse"/>
            <fault name="CISFault" message="cis:OperationException"/>
        </operation>
        <operation name="processTenderUpdate">
            <documentation>Update the tender information after the load has been tendered or tender accepted. This operation may invoke Routing, Rating and Scheduling.</documentation>
            <input message="cis:processTenderUpdate"/>
            <output message="cis:processTenderUpdateResponse"/>
            <fault name="CISFault" message="cis:OperationException"/>
        </operation>
        <operation name="processTenderAccept">
            <documentation>Accept tenders for existing loads. Advances the load status from Tendered to Tender Accepted. The transaction may fail if Transportation Manager is unavailable, or if there is an error in the request. An error message will be published on the front bus.</documentation>
            <input message="cis:processTenderAccept"/>
            <output message="cis:processTenderAcceptResponse"/>
            <fault name="CISFault" message="cis:OperationException"/>
        </operation>
        <operation name="processTenderReject">
            <documentation>Rejects tenders for existing loads by advancing their status to from Tendered to Tender Rejected. The transaction may fail if Transportation Manager is unavailable, or if there is an error in the request. An error message will be published on the front bus.</documentation>
            <input message="cis:processTenderReject"/>
            <output message="cis:processTenderRejectResponse"/>
            <fault name="CISFault" message="cis:OperationException"/>
        </operation>
        <operation name="processAutoTender">
            <documentation>Start/stop/resume carrier sequential tendering process for an existing load.</documentation>
            <input message="cis:processAutoTender"/>
            <output message="cis:processAutoTenderResponse"/>
            <fault name="CISFault" message="cis:OperationException"/>
        </operation>
        <operation name="processLoadRetrieve">
            <documentation>Retrieves the contents of loads. The transaction may fail if Transportation Manager is unavailable, or if there is an error in the request. An error message will be published on the front bus.</documentation>
            <input message="cis:processLoadRetrieve"/>
            <output message="cis:processLoadRetrieveResponse"/>
            <fault name="CISFault" message="cis:OperationException"/>
        </operation>
        <operation name="processLoadSelect">
            <documentation>Retrieves the load ID of each load. These load IDs can be used to retrieve the Load structures using the processLoadRetrieve operation. The transaction may fail if Transportation Manager is unavailable, or if there is an error in the request. An error message will be published on the front bus.</documentation>
            <input message="cis:processLoadSelect"/>
            <output message="cis:processLoadSelectResponse"/>
            <fault name="CISFault" message="cis:OperationException"/>
        </operation>
        <operation name="processLoadReturnToOpen">
            <documentation>Returns the status of each load in LoadPlanList from Planned to Open. By default, this operation leaves the load unattached to any Plan. You can attach the load to a plan using the appropriate plan ID with the load ID in the LoadPlan collection. The only API operations that can attach a load to a plan are the processLoadCreate and processLoadReturnToOpen. There is no direct API operation to attach a load to a plan. The transaction may fail if Transportation Manager is unavailable, or if there is an error in the request. An error message will be published on the front bus.</documentation>
            <input message="cis:processLoadReturnToOpen"/>
            <output message="cis:processLoadReturnToOpenResponse"/>
            <fault name="CISFault" message="cis:OperationException"/>
        </operation>
        <operation name="processBookingReturnToOpen">
            <documentation>Returns the status of each booking from Planned or Tender Rejected to Open. This operation leaves all loads of the booking unattached to any Plan. The transaction may fail if Transportation Manager is unavailable, or if there is an error in the request. An error message will be published on the front bus.</documentation>
            <input message="cis:processBookingReturnToOpen"/>
            <output message="cis:processBookingReturnToOpenResponse"/>
            <fault name="CISFault" message="cis:OperationException"/>
        </operation>
        <operation name="processLoadReturnToPlanned">
            <documentation>Returns the status of each load in the load ID list from Tender Rejected to Planned. The transaction may fail if Transportation Manager is unavailable, or if there is an error in the request. An error message will be published on the front bus.</documentation>
            <input message="cis:processLoadReturnToPlanned"/>
            <output message="cis:processLoadReturnToPlannedResponse"/>
            <fault name="CISFault" message="cis:OperationException"/>
        </operation>
        <operation name="processBookingReturnToPlanned">
            <documentation>Returns the status of each booking from Tender Rejected to Planned. The transaction may fail if Transportation Manager is unavailable, or if there is an error in the request. An error message will be published on the front bus.</documentation>
            <input message="cis:processBookingReturnToPlanned"/>
            <output message="cis:processBookingReturnToPlannedResponse"/>
            <fault name="CISFault" message="cis:OperationException"/>
        </operation>
        <operation name="processBookingSetToPlanned">
            <documentation>Advances the status of each booking from Open to Planned. The transaction may fail if Transportation Manager is unavailable, or if there is an error in the request. An error message will be published on the front bus.</documentation>
            <input message="cis:processBookingSetToPlanned"/>
            <output message="cis:processBookingSetToPlannedResponse"/>
            <fault name="CISFault" message="cis:OperationException"/>
        </operation>
        <operation name="processBuildStop">
            <documentation>Build stops for each load in the load ID list and each load of the trips in the trip ID list. If the load already belongs to the trip in the trip ID list, do not include the load in the load ID list. Otherwise the operation will fail. The transaction may fail if Transportation Manager is unavailable, or if there is an error in the request. An error message will be published on the front bus.</documentation>
            <input message="cis:processBuildStop"/>
            <output message="cis:processBuildStopResponse"/>
            <fault name="CISFault" message="cis:OperationException"/>
        </operation>
        <operation name="processReSequenceStop">
            <documentation>Re-sequences stops for a load. The transaction may fail if Transportation Manager is unavailable, or if there is an error in the request. An error message will be published on the front bus.</documentation>
            <input message="cis:processReSequenceStop"/>
            <output message="cis:processReSequenceStopResponse"/>
            <fault name="CISFault" message="cis:OperationException"/>
        </operation>
        <operation name="processLoadConfirm">
            <documentation>Confirms specified loads. This operation may invoke Routing, Rating and Scheduling. The transaction may fail if Transportation Manager is unavailable, or if there is an error in the request. An error message will be published on the front bus.</documentation>
            <input message="cis:processLoadConfirm"/>
            <output message="cis:processLoadConfirmResponse"/>
            <fault name="CISFault" message="cis:OperationException"/>
        </operation>
        <operation name="processStopConfirm">
            <documentation>Confirms specified stops. This operation may invoke Routing, Rating and Scheduling. The transaction may fail if Transportation Manager is unavailable, or if there is an error in the request. An error message will be published on the front bus.</documentation>
            <input message="cis:processStopConfirm"/>
            <output message="cis:processStopConfirmResponse"/>
            <fault name="CISFault" message="cis:OperationException"/>
        </operation>
        <operation name="processStopDockCommitmentCreate">
            <documentation>Create dock commitment. The transaction may fail if Transportation Manager is unavailable, or if there is an error in the request. An error message will be published on the front bus.</documentation>
            <input message="cis:processStopDockCommitmentCreate"/>
            <output message="cis:processStopDockCommitmentCreateResponse"/>
            <fault name="CISFault" message="cis:OperationException"/>
        </operation>
        <operation name="processStopDockCommitmentDelete">
            <documentation>Delete dock commitment. The transaction may fail if Transportation Manager is unavailable, or if there is an error in the request. An error message will be published on the front bus.</documentation>
            <input message="cis:processStopDockCommitmentDelete"/>
            <output message="cis:processStopDockCommitmentDeleteResponse"/>
            <fault name="CISFault" message="cis:OperationException"/>
        </operation>
        <operation name="processStopDockCommitmentRetrieve">
            <documentation>Retrieve stop dock commitment. Not applicable if the dock commitment is not linked to a stop. The transaction may fail if Transportation Manager is unavailable, or if there is an error in the request. An error message will be published on the front bus.</documentation>
            <input message="cis:processStopDockCommitmentRetrieve"/>
            <output message="cis:processStopDockCommitmentRetrieveResponse"/>
            <fault name="CISFault" message="cis:OperationException"/>
        </operation>
        <operation name="processStopDockCommitmentUpdate">
            <documentation>Update dock commitment. The transaction may fail if Transportation Manager is unavailable, or if there is an error in the request. An error message will be published on the front bus.</documentation>
            <input message="cis:processStopDockCommitmentUpdate"/>
            <output message="cis:processStopDockCommitmentUpdateResponse"/>
            <fault name="CISFault" message="cis:OperationException"/>
        </operation>
        <operation name="processStopDockCommitmentGenerateEvent">
            <documentation>Generate event for dock commitment. The transaction may fail if Transportation Manager is unavailable, or if there is an error in the request. An error message will be published on the front bus.</documentation>
            <input message="cis:processStopDockCommitmentGenerateEvent"/>
            <output message="cis:processStopDockCommitmentGenerateEventResponse"/>
            <fault name="CISFault" message="cis:OperationException"/>
        </operation>
        <operation name="processStopDockCommitmentSwap">
            <documentation>Swaps two dock commitments. The transaction may fail if Transportation Manager is unavailable, or if there is an error in the request. An error message will be published on the front bus.</documentation>
            <input message="cis:processStopDockCommitmentSwap"/>
            <output message="cis:processStopDockCommitmentSwapResponse"/>
            <fault name="CISFault" message="cis:OperationException"/>
        </operation>
        <operation name="processLoadUpdateProgress">
            <documentation>Update the progress of existing loads by sending the list of events that describe the progress of the loads. You can specify the load to be updated by its Load ID, Load Tracking Number, Master BOL, or a Reference Number. The transaction may fail if Transportation Manager is unavailable, or if there is an error in the request. An error message will be published on the front bus.</documentation>
            <input message="cis:processLoadUpdateProgress"/>
            <output message="cis:processLoadUpdateProgressResponse"/>
            <fault name="CISFault" message="cis:OperationException"/>
        </operation>
        <operation name="processLoadUnSuspend">
            <documentation>Sets the given loads to be unsuspended. Will return an error if the load is not in suspended status. This operation may invoke Routing, Rating and Scheduling. The transaction may fail if Transportation Manager is unavailable, or if there is an error in the request. An error message will be published on the front bus.</documentation>
            <input message="cis:processLoadUnSuspend"/>
            <output message="cis:processLoadUnSuspendResponse"/>
            <fault name="CISFault" message="cis:OperationException"/>
        </operation>
        <operation name="processLoadSuspend">
            <documentation>Sets the given loads to be suspended. Will return an error if the load is not in suspended status. The transaction may fail if Transportation Manager is unavailable, or if there is an error in the request. An error message will be published on the front bus.</documentation>
            <input message="cis:processLoadSuspend"/>
            <output message="cis:processLoadSuspendResponse"/>
            <fault name="CISFault" message="cis:OperationException"/>
        </operation>
        <operation name="processLoadManifest">
            <documentation>Manifests existing loads. (A manifest is a grouping of shipment legs being sent from a single shipping point to other locations using a single carrier.) This operation may invoke Routing, Rating and Scheduling. The transaction may fail if Transportation Manager is unavailable, or if there is an error in the request. An error message will be published on the front bus.</documentation>
            <input message="cis:processLoadManifest"/>
            <output message="cis:processLoadManifestResponse"/>
            <fault name="CISFault" message="cis:OperationException"/>
        </operation>
        <operation name="processSetStopETA">
            <documentation>Sets the estimated time of arrivals (ETA) for the specified stops. The stop for which the estimated time of arrival is being set is identified in two steps: 1. The load is identified in the same way as in the processLoadUpdateProgressType operation. 2. The load's stop is identified in one of the following ways: by the shipping location code and type - if this is not unique for the load, then an error occurs and the service call will fail. by the stop sequential number The transaction may fail if Transportation Manager is unavailable, or if there is an error in the request. An error message will be published on the front bus.</documentation>
            <input message="cis:processSetStopETA"/>
            <output message="cis:processSetStopETAResponse"/>
            <fault name="CISFault" message="cis:OperationException"/>
        </operation>
        <operation name="processSetStopProofOfDelivery">
            <documentation>Sets Proof of Delivery (POD) information for the specified stops. The load and shipment leg that are completed at the specified stop must have a status of In Transit or Delivered. The stops are identified in the same way as in processSetStopETAType. The transaction may fail if Transportation Manager is unavailable, or if there is an error in the request. An error message will be published on the front bus.</documentation>
            <input message="cis:processSetStopProofOfDelivery"/>
            <output message="cis:processSetStopProofOfDeliveryResponse"/>
            <fault name="CISFault" message="cis:OperationException"/>
        </operation>
        <operation name="processSetStopToDelivered">
            <documentation>Sets the status of a stop of an existing load to Delivered. The load and shipment leg that are completed at the specified stop must have a status of In Transit. The stops are identified in the same way as in processSetStopETAType. The transaction may fail if Transportation Manager is unavailable, or if there is an error in the request. An error message will be published on the front bus.</documentation>
            <input message="cis:processSetStopToDelivered"/>
            <output message="cis:processSetStopToDeliveredResponse"/>
            <fault name="CISFault" message="cis:OperationException"/>
        </operation>
        <operation name="processSetShipmentToDelivered">
            <documentation>Sets the status of existing shipment legs to Delivered. The shipment legs are identified in the same way as in processShipmentUpdateProgressType. The transaction may fail if Transportation Manager is unavailable, or if there is an error in the request. An error message will be published on the front bus.</documentation>
            <input message="cis:processSetShipmentToDelivered"/>
            <output message="cis:processSetShipmentToDeliveredResponse"/>
            <fault name="CISFault" message="cis:OperationException"/>
        </operation>
        <operation name="processSetShipmentProofOfDelivery">
            <documentation>Sets the Proof of Delivery (POD) information for existing shipment legs. The shipment legs are identified the same way as in processShipmentUpdateProgressType. The transaction may fail if Transportation Manager is unavailable, or if there is an error in the request. An error message will be published on the front bus.</documentation>
            <input message="cis:processSetShipmentProofOfDelivery"/>
            <output message="cis:processSetShipmentProofOfDeliveryResponse"/>
            <fault name="CISFault" message="cis:OperationException"/>
        </operation>
        <operation name="processStopReturnToDelivered">
            <documentation>Returns the status of a stop of an existing load to Delivered. At least one shipment leg that is completed at the specified stop must have a status of POD. The stops are identified in the same way as in processSetStopETAType. The transaction may fail if Transportation Manager is unavailable, or if there is an error in the request. An error message will be published on the front bus.</documentation>
            <input message="cis:processStopReturnToDelivered"/>
            <output message="cis:processStopReturnToDeliveredResponse"/>
            <fault name="CISFault" message="cis:OperationException"/>
        </operation>
        <operation name="processStopReturnToInTransit">
            <documentation>Returns the status of a stop of an existing load to In Transit. At least one shipment leg that is completed at the specified stop must have a status of Delivered or POD. The stops are identified in the same way as in processSetStopETAType. The transaction may fail if Transportation Manager is unavailable, or if there is an error in the request. An error message will be published on the front bus.</documentation>
            <input message="cis:processStopReturnToInTransit"/>
            <output message="cis:processStopReturnToInTransitResponse"/>
            <fault name="CISFault" message="cis:OperationException"/>
        </operation>
        <operation name="processShipmentReturnToDelivered">
            <documentation>Returns the status of existing shipment legs to Delivered. The shipment legs are identified in the same way as in processShipmentUpdateProgress. The transaction may fail if Transportation Manager is unavailable, or if there is an error in the request. An error message will be published on the front bus.</documentation>
            <input message="cis:processShipmentReturnToDelivered"/>
            <output message="cis:processShipmentReturnToDeliveredResponse"/>
            <fault name="CISFault" message="cis:OperationException"/>
        </operation>
        <operation name="processShipmentReturnToInTransit">
            <documentation>Returns the status of existing shipment legs to In Transit. The shipment legs are identified in the same way as in processShipmentUpdateProgress. The transaction may fail if Transportation Manager is unavailable, or if there is an error in the request. An error message will be published on the front bus.</documentation>
            <input message="cis:processShipmentReturnToInTransit"/>
            <output message="cis:processShipmentReturnToInTransitResponse"/>
            <fault name="CISFault" message="cis:OperationException"/>
        </operation>
        <operation name="processShipmentUpdateProgress">
            <documentation>Updates the progress information for existing shipment legs. The shipment and shipment leg must be in a status of In Transit. The shipment leg is identified in the following way: 1. The shipment is identified by its Shipment ID, Shipment Tracking Number, a Reference Number, or a combination of Shipment Tracking Number and Division or Reference Number, and Division. 2. After the shipment is determined, the shipment leg should be identified in it. The shipment leg can be identified by the BOL number, the shipment leg ID, or the shipment leg sequential number. The transaction may fail if Transportation Manager is unavailable, or if there is an error in the request. An error message will be published on the front bus.</documentation>
            <input message="cis:processShipmentUpdateProgress"/>
            <output message="cis:processShipmentUpdateProgressResponse"/>
            <fault name="CISFault" message="cis:OperationException"/>
        </operation>
        <operation name="processShipmentConfirm">
            <documentation>Confirms existing shipments legs. This operation may invoke Routing, Rating and Scheduling. If Routing, Rating and Scheduling failed, the operation may indicate the operation completed successfully but with a Warning message. In this case, the shipment legs are not actually confirmed. If the carrier, service, trailer equipment type and tractor equipment type provided in the request differ from those of the shipment leg, the related attributes on the shipment leg may be updated. The transaction may fail if Transportation Manager is unavailable, or if there is an error in the request. An error message will be published on the front bus.</documentation>
            <input message="cis:processShipmentConfirm"/>
            <output message="cis:processShipmentConfirmResponse"/>
            <fault name="CISFault" message="cis:OperationException"/>
        </operation>
        <operation name="processShipmentLegActuals">
            <documentation>Updates, reports and/or reverses the Report Details. The transaction may fail if Transportation Manager is unavailable, or if there is an error in the request. An error message will be published on the front bus.</documentation>
            <input message="cis:processShipmentLegActuals"/>
            <output message="cis:processShipmentLegActualsResponse"/>
            <fault name="CISFault" message="cis:OperationException"/>
        </operation>
        <operation name="processRetrieveProofOfDeliveryInformation">
            <documentation>Retrieves proof of delivery information. The transaction may fail if Transportation Manager is unavailable, or if there is an error in the request. An error message will be published on the front bus.</documentation>
            <input message="cis:processRetrieveProofOfDeliveryInformation"/>
            <output message="cis:processRetrieveProofOfDeliveryInformationResponse"/>
            <fault name="CISFault" message="cis:OperationException"/>
        </operation>
        <operation name="processShipmentLegContainerUpdateProgress">
            <documentation>Updates the progress information for a shipment leg container. The transaction may fail if Transportation Manager is unavailable, or if there is an error in the request. An error message will be published on the front bus.</documentation>
            <input message="cis:processShipmentLegContainerUpdateProgress"/>
            <output message="cis:processShipmentLegContainerUpdateProgressResponse"/>
            <fault name="CISFault" message="cis:OperationException"/>
        </operation>
        <operation name="processSetShipmentLegContainerToDelivered">
            <documentation>Sets the status of a shipment leg container to Delivered. The transaction may fail if Transportation Manager is unavailable, or if there is an error in the request. An error message will be published on the front bus.</documentation>
            <input message="cis:processSetShipmentLegContainerToDelivered"/>
            <output message="cis:processSetShipmentLegContainerToDeliveredResponse"/>
            <fault name="CISFault" message="cis:OperationException"/>
        </operation>
        <operation name="processSetShipmentLegContainerProofOfDelivery">
            <documentation>Sets the Proof of Delivery (POD) information for a shipment leg container. The transaction may fail if Transportation Manager is unavailable, or if there is an error in the request. An error message will be published on the front bus.</documentation>
            <input message="cis:processSetShipmentLegContainerProofOfDelivery"/>
            <output message="cis:processSetShipmentLegContainerProofOfDeliveryResponse"/>
            <fault name="CISFault" message="cis:OperationException"/>
        </operation>
        <operation name="processShipmentLegContainerReturnToDelivered">
            <documentation>Returns the status of a shipment leg container to Delivered. The transaction may fail if Transportation Manager is unavailable, or if there is an error in the request. An error message will be published on the front bus.</documentation>
            <input message="cis:processShipmentLegContainerReturnToDelivered"/>
            <output message="cis:processShipmentLegContainerReturnToDeliveredResponse"/>
            <fault name="CISFault" message="cis:OperationException"/>
        </operation>
        <operation name="processShipmentLegContainerReturnToInTransit">
            <documentation>Returns the status of a shipment leg container to In Transit. The transaction may fail if Transportation Manager is unavailable, or if there is an error in the request. An error message will be published on the front bus.</documentation>
            <input message="cis:processShipmentLegContainerReturnToInTransit"/>
            <output message="cis:processShipmentLegContainerReturnToInTransitResponse"/>
            <fault name="CISFault" message="cis:OperationException"/>
        </operation>
        <operation name="processContainerTrackingNumberUpdate">
            <documentation>Updates container tracking number for a shipment leg container. The transaction may fail if Transportation Manager is unavailable, or if there is an error in the request. An error message will be published on the front bus.</documentation>
            <input message="cis:processContainerTrackingNumberUpdate"/>
            <output message="cis:processContainerTrackingNumberUpdateResponse"/>
            <fault name="CISFault" message="cis:OperationException"/>
        </operation>
        <operation name="processAddressFormat">
            <documentation>Formats an address. The transaction may fail if Transportation Manager is unavailable, or if there is an error in the request. An error message will be published on the front bus.</documentation>
            <input message="cis:processAddressFormat"/>
            <output message="cis:processAddressFormatResponse"/>
            <fault name="CISFault" message="cis:OperationException"/>
        </operation>
        <operation name="processAddressValidate">
            <documentation>Validates addresses. The transaction may fail if Transportation Manager is unavailable, or if there is an error in the request. An error message will be published on the front bus.</documentation>
            <input message="cis:processAddressValidate"/>
            <output message="cis:processAddressValidateResponse"/>
            <fault name="CISFault" message="cis:OperationException"/>
        </operation>
        <operation name="processPostalDataAdd">
            <documentation>Adds records to postal data used for address search and validation. Only one user at a time can perform postal/city data modifications for a country. Database privileges to update postal/city data are required. The transaction may fail if Transportation Manager is unavailable, or if there is an error in the request. An error message will be published on the front bus.</documentation>
            <input message="cis:processPostalDataAdd"/>
            <output message="cis:processPostalDataAddResponse"/>
            <fault name="CISFault" message="cis:OperationException"/>
        </operation>
        <operation name="processPostalCodeRangesRebuild">
